<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick the Fair</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1289–1330</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Frederick I of Austria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick the Fair was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> from 1308 and German anti-king from 1314, elected by one faction against Louis IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. Defeated and captured by Louis at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-muhldorf">Battle of Mühldorf</a> in 1322, he was held prisoner until 1325, when the two rivals agreed to share the royal title. He had little real power thereafter and died in 1330.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-the-fair.jpg" alt="Frederick the Fair" width="320" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl von Sava · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slicny2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
